# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# 1. Legacy .html paths -> clean routes, as real HTTP 301s.
#    These are the paths the site has shipped for years, so they are still linked
#    from outside (old blog posts, Google Business Profile, printed material).
#    A 301 is a server response: a client-side <Navigate> redirect would look
#    identical to a visitor but tells a crawler nothing, so these MUST live here.
#    Keep this list in sync with LEGACY_REDIRECTS in src/content/site.ts.
#
# 2. SPA fallback last: every clean path is a client-side route, so anything not
#    matched above must serve the shell rather than a 404. Netlify rewrites the
#    URL, so the canonical tags in src/hooks/useDocumentMeta.ts remain correct.

